newfoundland here is only a recent  addition to canada  having joined it in 1949. yet canada was  confederated in 1867 and so the two  remain divided for nearly a century  which raises a pretty obvious question  why why did it take so long for  newfoundland to join canada  so when the colonies which would become  canada were debating confederation in  1864  politicians in newfoundland began to  discuss the issue at home did they want  to be a part of this new canada and take  their rightful place in the world or  just sit on the sidelines and watch  history pass them by  turns out the sidelines were just fine  and newfoundland would sit this canada  thing out  their primary reasons were that one  whilst the politicians there were  largely pro-confederation the people  were most certainly not  which brings us on to reason number two  catholics  specifically french catholics who made a  precisely chunk of this new canada's  population and thus had a lot of  influence  and the people of newfoundland proud  protestants that they were were having  none of that  and the third reason was economic  newfoundland had low taxes and there  were concerns that a new central  government in ottawa would raise them to  pay for things like railways and a  national military  so what changed well newfoundland  continued to develop on its own and its  people for the most part still wish to  remain independent there was a very  sudden change of heart in 1895 when the  newfoundland premier william whiteway  made a plea to join the confederation  and this was totally because they loved  canada and nothing to do with the  massive financial crisis that had just  hit them  the canadians said no and so they were  left to struggle on with mountains of  debt  after this the people of newfoundland  were still against confederation and in  1907 newfoundland was promoted from a  colony to a dominion  meaning that its continued independence  seemed assured and its history largely  mirrored those of the other dominions  throughout the early 20th century there  were reforms at home political scandals  world war 1 greater exploitation of  natural resources and a general  improvement in the economic situation  that was at least until the great  depression which could only mean one  thing  pain newfoundland was essentially  bankrupted by this and so it went for  the previous tactic of trying to sell  itself to canada  the canadians said no because it sounded  expensive and the british refused to  help unless newfoundland suspended its  government and let them run it instead  which they did in 1934 and the british  took over before proceeding to also be  terrible at running the place  so in world war ii the british  negotiated away basing rights to the  united states in return for some much  needed ships and the americans began  massive investment in the area  this drastically improved the living  standards of the people living there and  after the war many people demanded that  british rule come to an end which meant  it was time for a referendum  the people had two choices go back to  being independent or remain  under british control the first option  terrified the british because it would  have meant newfoundland increasing its  ties with the united states and there  were some there even advocating for  statehood  this option also terrified the canadians  because with these borders canada's  access to the atlantic could be  restricted  and along with it britain's access to  canadian resources  and so to stop this potential outcome  from happening the british and canadians  teamed up to add a third option to the  ballot  join canada now the representatives of  newfoundland didn't want this option but  that's not how british rule worked and  so  on the ballot it went the referendum was  held in 1948 and whichever option gained  50  of the vote that would be the action  taken but none of them won and so a  second referendum this time without the  potential to continue british rule was  held and union with canada won with 52  percent of the vote  and after some negotiations newfoundland  ceased to exist as a nation and became a  part of canada the next year  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bisonette kelly money maker alex  schwinn mr wolfe captain cydog adam  stalter  skye chappelle marvin casou aaron the  white mo  james castaneda jordan longley jerry  landon gustav swan rasheed ali winston k  wood boogerly wiggily spinning three  plates coppertone maggie paskowski  spencer lightfoot matthew shipley robert  wetzel corso wolff the mc whopper  anthony beckett marcus asner lil brep  and tc and charles the first
 

